[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
I tested connectivity from multiple Office VLAN hosts (192.168.3.x) to several destinations beyond the office gateway and all paths are healthy. From office_pc (192.168.3.2), ICMP to the Server Room (pc1: 1.0.0.5) succeeded with 0% loss and ~1.4 ms RTT; to the Internet Lab (pc3: 128.168.0.3) also succeeded with 0% loss and ~1.5 ms RTT. Additional office hosts (enquiry, exam_cell, tpo) can all reach the server (1.0.0.5) without loss. From office_pc, pings to other departments (CS: 192.168.2.2 and IT: 192.168.1.2) also succeed with low RTT. These results prove that inter-VLAN routing across the intermediate routers and links is currently functioning end to end. If any “middle” router were down, these probes would show 100% loss or clear asymmetry, which they do not.

Localization: No evidence of failure on router0/router1/router2 or their interlinks; traffic traverses between Office, Servers, Internet Lab, CS, and IT segments normally.

Root cause: Unable to reproduce the reported outage; no device failure found—likely a transient or host-local issue that has since cleared.

Corrective fix: No network changes required. Advise users to capture traceroute and ping results during any recurrence and check local host factors (NIC state, DHCP/ARP, host firewall). We will continue monitoring, but as of now the routed core and L2 segments are operational. 
=== END ===